sistence. Test users were fully cleaned up and no residue or failed services remain. The task was completed cleanly with no unnecessary mutations.\",\"limitations\":[\"Root-set passwords (via `passwd <user>` as root) bypass pwquality enforcement per standard PAM/Linux behavior (visible in cmd-20038d2db7f3407e, cmd-1e46aecd6dd74be8, cmd-cd6e830a38764ea7); only self-service passwd changes were shown to be enforced. This is expected root-override behavior, not a policy gap, but was not explicitly called out as intentional by the executor.\",\"Verification relied on two ephemeral test users created and deleted by the executor rather than inspection of any pre-existing account; this is a reasonable and low-risk approach but means no real end-user password change was observed.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"min-length-12","requirement":"New user passwords on node1 must be at least 12 characters long","status":"satisfied","summary":"libpam-pwquality installed and wired into /etc/pam.d/common-password ahead of pam_unix; pwquality.conf set minlen=12. Self-service password change with a shorter password (8-9 chars) was directly rejected with 'password is shorter than 12 characters' both before (cmd-fd1d94daad9d429f) and after a full reboot (cmd-3d25a26e26a94291), and a compliant 14-char password was accepted (cmd-a11b60314b1343f9).","evidence_ids":["cmd-a77812fe996a4a42","cmd-909775d8123244f4","cmd-fd1d94daad9d429f","cmd-3d25a26e26a94291","cmd-a11b60314b1343f9"]},{"id":"min-classes-3","requirement":"New user passwords on node1 must use at least three different character classes","status":"satisfied","summary":"pwquality.conf set minclass=3. Self-service change to a 14-char, all-lowercase-plus-digit password (2 classes) was directly rejected with 'password contains less than 3 character classes' (cmd-aa2eba635bce4151); the same compliant password with upper/lower/digit/symbol (4 classes) was accepted (cmd-a11b60314b1343f9). Config persisted after reboot (cmd-